# landing-cli:start
# Written by @wisent-ai/landing-cli with the site. Audit exclusions for
# `tama find-violations`: paths fixed by something outside this project.
#
# The repository root. npm reads package.json and package-lock.json, tsc
# reads tsconfig.json, Next reads next.config.ts and rewrites next-env.d.ts
# on every build, the design lint reads .wisent-design-lint.json, git reads
# .gitignore, GitHub reads README.md, and landing-cli reads the brief, the
# config, the component plan, the plan and the manifest as landing.*.json in
# the site root. The stylesheet is emitted as parts under src/styles and the
# page code under src/app, so nothing here is a module that could move.
.
#
# The generated content. src/content holds the brief-derived JSON the page
# reads at build time — one file per kind, each replaced whole on every run —
# and src/styles holds the stylesheet parts. Neither is a folder somebody
# navigates by hand, and a sixth kind of content is not a reason to invent a
# sub-folder the reader would then have to follow.
src/content/
src/styles/
#
# The fonts. A family ships one file per weight and width, the foundry
# decides how many, and the CSS references each by that exact name.
public/fonts/
#
# The page directory. Its file names are Next's contract, not a module
# layout: layout.tsx and page.tsx are the route, robots.ts and sitemap.ts are
# the two files Next serves from those names, and the icons are served from
# theirs. Nested routes are already sub-folders.
src/app
#
# One stylesheet, emitted whole. A site generated before the stylesheet was
# split into parts carries it here and its layout imports it, so its length
# is the length of the design tokens plus the component rules that page uses.
# A site generated now has the parts under src/styles instead and no file at
# this path at all.
src/app/globals.css
#
# The documentation. The docs pipeline shares this repository with the
# landing page: it writes src/app/docs and the content modules under
# src/lib/docs, where a page is a document rather than a module — its length
# is the length of the documentation it carries, and it is replaced whole on
# every publish. The same reasoning the operator applied to manuscripts.
src/lib/docs/
# landing-cli:end
